{{!
	Bottom dock: a fixed-position menu anchored to the bottom of the viewport.
	Rendered last in skin.mustache, after the page container and the sticky header container.
	Styled by resources/skins.notion.js/bottomDock.less, which targets the core-owned portlet
	classes below; this partial therefore adds no presentational class of its own.

	object|null data-portlets.data-dock-bottom the "dock-bottom" portlet from core's
		standardised data-portlets structure. Its items are contributed by extensions and
		gadgets through mw.util.addPortletLink with the p-dock-bottom target, so on a
		default install the portlet arrives carrying no items and the list renders empty.
		The guard below additionally means that a data set which omits the portlet
		altogether emits no markup whatsoever, rather than an empty fixed-position shell.
	string class core-owned portlet classes, e.g. "mw-portlet mw-portlet-dock-bottom", with
		"emptyPortlet" appended while the dock holds no items. Passed through verbatim: the
		class is owned by core, not by the skin, and is the styling and scripting hook.
	string id core-owned portlet id, "p-dock-bottom". Passed through verbatim: it is the
		public target of mw.util.addPortletLink and thus part of the DOM contract.
	object[] array-items one record per dock item, each carrying html-item.
	string array-items.html-item pre-rendered list-item markup for a single dock item,
		emitted unescaped so the surrounding list keeps only list-item children.
}}
{{#data-portlets.data-dock-bottom}}
<div class="{{ class }}" id="{{id}}">
	<ul>
		{{#array-items}}{{{html-item}}}{{/array-items}}
	</ul>
</div>
{{/data-portlets.data-dock-bottom}}
